  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "West Kittanning was founded in 1855 by John Cunningham and was once called Bellville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://westkittanningpa.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s name comes from the Lenape word “Kithanink,” meaning “the main place,” highlighting its historic Native American roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/west-kittanning-73344"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Perched on a hilltop, West Kittanning overlooks the Allegheny River, offering sweeping views of the surrounding valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Kittanning%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Though it shares many milestones with neighboring Kittanning, West Kittanning has maintained a separate municipal government since its early days.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/west-kittanning-73344"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In the past, the local economy was driven by coal mining and steel production, mirroring the broader industrial boom of Western Pennsylvania.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/west-kittanning-73344"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "West Kittanning sits about 40 miles northeast of Pittsburgh, placing it within easy reach of the city’s cultural and economic activities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
